  <prompt>
    Build the briefing-accuracy eval family: a mixed-item corpus that asserts ZERO cross-item pairing (title/regarding/citation always same item), plus aggregation-preference, grounding round-trip, and TL;DR-abstraction cases. Wire the eval suite as a required CI merge gate and add unit tests for the deterministic channel renderer. Per FR-A7 / NFR-02.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer + test architect. Follow ADR-038 test shapes strictly. Expert in the golden-utterance eval harness and the DailyBriefing deterministic pipeline.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A briefing-accuracy eval family exists with: (1) a mixed-item corpus asserting zero cross-item pairing including at least one case that would FAIL under the old cross-pairing bug and PASSES now; (2) aggregation-preference cases; (3) grounding round-trip cases (TL;DR facts trace to the deterministic view model); (4) TL;DR-abstraction cases (non-resolving anchor dropped). The eval suite is a required merge gate. The deterministic channel renderer has unit tests. All green.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The existing golden-utterances.json schema is dispatch-oriented (cases[] with caseId/family/channel/utterance/context/expected/assertions) and cannot express item-level accuracy assertions. A briefing-accuracy corpus likely needs its own fixture + suite. This family is the machine-verifiable proof that the R5 accuracy work holds and becomes the D-8 harness fixture source (FR-D1). It gates merges per NFR-02.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>tests/integration/contract/Eval/golden-utterances.json</file>
      <file>tests/integration/contract/Eval/GoldenUtteranceEvalSuiteTests.cs</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Ai/Narrators/DailyBriefingCollectorTests.cs</file>
      <file>.github/workflows/sdap-ci.yml</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/components/NarrativeCitedText.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The mixed-item corpus MUST assert ZERO cross-item pairing: for each item, title, regarding record name, and citation/link all originate from the SAME item. Include at least one case constructed so it would FAIL under the pre-R5 cross-pairing bug and PASSES after tasks 011/013/014.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The family MUST include aggregation-preference cases (the briefing prefers an aggregate "you have N …" over enumerating), grounding round-trip cases (every TL;DR fact traces to the deterministic view model), and TL;DR-abstraction cases (a non-resolving anchor is dropped, not warned).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">New tests land at KEEP paths per the 6 KEEP categories. Do NOT add banned shapes (Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, DI-registration-only tests, ctor null-check tests). Integration-heavy pyramid.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The eval suite MUST be a required merge check in CI (NFR-02). Wire it into .github/workflows/sdap-ci.yml as a required gate, not an advisory step.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Add unit tests for the deterministic channel renderer (task-011 output) — a row renders from a single item; the link target equals the item's link.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKE-PLAYBOOK-LLM-OUTPUT-PATTERN.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Golden-utterance eval suite" location="tests/integration/contract/Eval/GoldenUtteranceEvalSuiteTests.cs">
        The existing dispatch-oriented suite is the harness precedent. The briefing-accuracy corpus is a NEW fixture + suite (item-level assertions) alongside it — design the schema, don't force-fit the dispatch schema.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm tasks 011/013/014 have landed (deterministic rows, deterministic TL;DR scaffolding, itemRefs[] drop logic) so the corpus can assert against real behavior.</step>
    <step order="2">Design a briefing-accuracy fixture schema that expresses item-level assertions (per-item title/regarding/citation provenance, aggregate preference, grounding round-trip, anchor drop). If the dispatch schema cannot express these, create a new fixture file + suite (see escalation).</step>
    <step order="3">Author the mixed-item corpus incl. a case that FAILS under the old cross-pairing bug and PASSES now; add aggregation-preference, grounding round-trip, and TL;DR-abstraction cases.</step>
    <step order="4">Add unit tests for the deterministic channel renderer (single-item row; link target equals item link).</step>
    <step order="5">Wire the eval suite as a REQUIRED merge check in .github/workflows/sdap-ci.yml.</step>
    <step order="6">Run the full suite locally; confirm all green and the merge gate is required.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 016 completed. Record the schema decision + any deviations in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the existing golden-utterances.json schema cannot express item-level accuracy assertions, STOP and propose a NEW fixture format + suite (documented in notes) rather than force-fitting the dispatch-oriented schema. Present the proposed schema for confirmation before mass-authoring cases.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Run the eval + unit suites</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Run the renderer Jest tests</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Edit CI workflow</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Eval/briefing-accuracy-corpus.json</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Eval/BriefingAccuracyEvalSuiteTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/src/components/__tests__/deterministicRenderer.test.tsx</output>
    <output type="config">.github/workflows/sdap-ci.yml</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A mixed-item corpus exists asserting zero cross-item pairing, including ≥1 case that would FAIL under the old cross-pairing bug and PASSES now.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The family includes aggregation-preference, grounding round-trip, and TL;DR-abstraction (non-resolving anchor dropped) cases, all passing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The eval suite is a REQUIRED merge check in .github/workflows/sdap-ci.yml (not advisory).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The deterministic channel renderer has unit tests (single-item row; link target equals item link) that pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No banned test shapes are introduced (ADR-038); new tests land at KEEP paths.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The full eval + unit suite runs green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    See spec.md FR-A7 / NFR-02 and plan.md Phase A.7. Depends on 011/013/014. The corpus is reused as D-8 harness fixtures (FR-D1). Existing eval schema fields: caseId/family/channel/utterance/context/expected/assertions (dispatch-oriented) — item-level accuracy likely needs a new fixture per the plan Risk register. TEST-MODIFYING rigor applies.
  </notes>

